<section class="section wrap">
	<h1>Close racing, whatever your level</h1>
	<p class="lede">You're scored against your own predicted time, calculated from a qualifying round, so the fastest rider doesn't always win. Get your friends together, ride when it suits you, and let the league work out the scores.</p>
	<div class="actions">
		<a class="button" href="#join">Start a league</a>
		<a class="button button-outline" href="#how">How it works</a>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="how">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2>How it works</h2>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li><strong>Get your friends together</strong> Pick a group, set up a Strava club, and decide how often you want to race.</li>
			<li><strong>Ride a qualifier</strong> Everyone rides the same route once, flat out. Your time sets your predicted time for each race.</li>
			<li><strong>Race whenever suits you</strong> Each race is a set route with a window, usually two weeks.</li>
			<li><strong>Let the league do the maths</strong> Times are compared with each rider's prediction, points are awarded, and the standings update.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<h2>Why it's fair</h2>
	<p>Your qualifier shows how you ride on climbs, on the flat and in sprints. Each race is a <span class="badge badge-flat">flat</span>, <span class="badge badge-rolling">rolling</span> or <span class="badge badge-climbing">climbing</span> route, and your prediction adjusts to match. If you beat your prediction by more than anyone else, you win, even if you were last over the line.</p>
	<p>Your prediction moves a little after every race. Get fitter and you'll still be rewarded, and anyone who took it easy in the qualifier soon gets found out.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<h2>Points</h2>
	<p>Everyone who finishes scores something. Points go to the best results against prediction, with small gaps between places, so turning up always counts. There are bonus points for the fastest riders on the climbs and sprints, so the quickest riders still have something to chase.</p>
	<p>Each league sets its own points to suit how many people are riding.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<div class="section-head">
		<h2>The rules</h2>
		<p class="section-note">League pages are private and only show initials, places, points and how far each rider beat their own prediction. Times are never published.</p>
	</div>
	<ol class="rules">
		<li class="panel"><strong>Ride solo</strong> No group rides, races or events, because drafting breaks the handicap.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Ride the set route</strong> Flat out, within the window. Your best effort counts.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Keep Strava sync on</strong> And check your first ride shows up.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Join your league's Strava club</strong> So you appear on the leaderboard.</li>
		<li class="panel"><strong>Be honest</strong> Use an honest weight and height, and a smart trainer or power meter if you can.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

